{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"cec7ca988648b8e7164bb9ff70db290e45c5176db8bdeba85849b0ef0449623e","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_b176ef168dc7257d145a3611fc78db6b49d5d20d3867f1fb00bf2ad5672c7556","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical evaluation of defensive methods for deep neural networks. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance, privacy, anonymity, or plagiarism judgments, as the text lacks explicit statements regarding data licensing, ethical review, or submission policies.","paper_id":"ByToKu9ll","paper_identity_sha256":"f9ac806067f7336accf141f65e891d40b7d793fbb45c86ac8f0855a58f67e680","prompt_identity_sha256":"f810b920bd68a5b8e626d28396f600fda058164d3c4eb8da2d616ff420999702","raw_response_sha256":"3a95ca8df5a8941396081397f79da6d932377267e7c3a5305f1b5ddb8f8f5b7e","request_identity_sha256":"da9415cc816fd93f1c00b41e3dba569c8607e772d3a1c28befc4ea89d7c9a008","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"a599b945e96314349ad1d15f79431746accaf2d32375eb1bc88b18dee67dfecd","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009"],"review_text":"The paper identifies a material ethical risk pathway by describing how adversarial examples can be used to manipulate safety-critical systems, specifically citing the example of manipulating stop signs in autonomous driving to cause accidents. However, the paper does not provide a dedicated discussion on ethical mitigation strategies, fairness, or broader societal harms beyond the technical evaluation of defensive robustness. The focus remains on algorithmic performance rather than responsible AI deployment considerations.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the MNIST and CIFAR-10 datasets for its experiments. The text does not contain explicit statements regarding data licensing, consent, or privacy compliance for these specific datasets. As these are standard public benchmarks, no visible privacy violations or misuse of restricted data are apparent in the provided text, but the absence of explicit compliance documentation means the supplied evidence is insufficient to fully determine data usage policy adherence.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Xinyun Chen, Bo Li, Yevgeniy Vorobeychik) and their institutional affiliations (Shanghai Jiao Tong University, University of Michigan, Vanderbilt University) on the title page. While this is standard for published versions, the corpus build lacks a frozen venue-specific anonymity policy for the 2017 ICLR submission to determine if this constitutes a double-blind violation. Therefore, the visible identification is noted, but no policy violation or clearance can be declared based on the supplied evidence.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied paper text does not contain explicit disclosures of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The corpus build does not include frozen external evidence or plagiarism overlap data to audit the originality of the content against other works. Consequently, the supplied evidence is insufficient to determine whether the paper is free from plagiarism or dual submission issues.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. The corpus build does not provide a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for the 2017 ICLR venue. Therefore, the absence of these items cannot be judged as a compliance failure, and the supplied evidence is insufficient to determine policy-required documentation adherence.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":